{"name":"Herb","hex":"#708452","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Herb","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A diminutive of the male given name Herbert."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Herb"}],"entries":[{"title":"Herb","blocks":[{"text":"Herbs are a widely distributed and widespread group of plants, excluding vegetables, with savory or aromatic properties that are used for flavoring and garnishing food, for medicinal purposes, or for fragrances. Culinary use typically distinguishes herbs from spices. Herbs generally refers to the leafy green or flowering parts of a plant, while spices are usually dried and produced from other parts of the plant, including seeds, bark, roots and fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Garden_of_herbs.jpg/330px-Garden_of_herbs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herb","wikidata":"Q207123"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/The_Herb_Garden_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1629279.jpg/500px-The_Herb_Garden_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1629279.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/The_Herb_Garden_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1629279.jpg/500px-The_Herb_Garden_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1629279.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Herb garden at Hardwick Hall, Derbyshire, England, originally planted in the 1870s by Lady Louisa Egerton, recreated by the National Trust, largely following the original design.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Herb_Garden_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1629279.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Thyme-Bundle.jpg/500px-Thyme-Bundle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm